 The 100-meter backstroke is slower than the 100-meter freestyle by 4 seconds, so it must take David 48 + 4 = 52 seconds to swim. The 100-meter butterfly is slower than the 100-meter backstroke by 3 seconds, so it must take David 52 + 3 = 55 seconds to swim. The 100-meter breaststroke is slower than the 100-meter butterfly by 2 seconds, so it must take David 55 + 2 = 57 seconds to swim. Therefore, the total time it takes David to swim all four events is 48 + 52 + 55 + 57 = 212 seconds.. The answer is 212.

